      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for perl-Data-Dump-Streamer",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for perl-Data-Dump-Streamer fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in perl-Data-Dump-Streamer:\n\nUpdated to 3.1.0 (3.001):\n\nSee /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-Data-Dump-Streamer/Changes\n\n3.001 - 2026-11-10:\n\n- Perltidy source to my preferred format. Fixed issues serializing\n  the global stash. Added test to detect if serializing the global\n  stash breaks anything.\n- Fix version assignments so PAUSE can index the distribution.\n\n3.00 - 2026-11-10:\n\n- Rewrite the dumping engine in C/XS, with AI assistance, for improved speed,\n  correctness and compatibility with Perl's refcounted stack. Improve Unicode\n  and regexp handling, and add experimental support for XPerl class objects.\n  (CVE-2026-126673 bsc#1290113)\n\n- Require Perl 5.18 or newer and a C compiler. Replace Module::Build with\n  ExtUtils::MakeMaker.\n\n- There is no pure-Perl version. Please don't upgrade if you need pure-Perl\n  support.\n\n- Normalize CPAN version\n  See https://github.com/openSUSE/cpanspec/issues/47 for details\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
